ls  for  the computational experiments namely  our  one led one lf and 2nf  note that these models have similar  structures uh in the sense that their  feasible regions are all matching  polytopes therefore both frankfurt  algorithm and cutting plane can handle  them efficiently  we consider several scenarios here  um we consider two scenarios for the  utility mattresses one is where the  utility matrices are bi-valued we call  them binary and the other case is where  utilities are general integers so we  call them non-binary  we also  consider different number of agents  and goods  from 200 of all the way to 2000  i have discarded the smaller instances  because the running times are negligible  here  we have also  considered different parameters to  capture the sparsity of the utility  mattresses through this parameter row  so the smaller value for row means  the in sense is sparser  uh from these results we can observe  that frank wolf can handle the binary  cases uh consistently uh more  efficiently than  the  cutting plane algorithm  while  both frank wolf and cutting plane are  suitable for the non-binary case  with a cutting plane performing slightly  better  than  the frank wolf particularly in the  denser  cases  now with then  with the  non-linear utility functions um one sad  and one nad we have considered a  different  number of agents and different segments  for the utility functions  for the separable case  capital k denotes the number of segments  for each pair of agent and good and we  have considered two numbers and for the  non-severable case it captures the  number of uh  segments for each agent  as expected we can observe that as we  increase the number of segments the  problem becomes increasingly more  challenging but  the cutting plane algorithm  has managed to solve all the instances  in  a few minutes  but with  the non-separable case it turns out that  the problem is more challenging that  than the separable case  and um but the cutting plane algorithm  solves  all the large instances um up to optimal  um solution  in less than one hour and uh but it  it starts to struggle for  the cases where the number of segments  are  larger  so uh  with this i end my talk thank you for  your attention  and we would be happy to hear your  questions
 

